From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] security/intel/cbnt: Use SHA-384 for KM public key hash on
 11th-gen+

Intel documents that for platforms starting with the 11th generation
(Meteor Lake included) the Boot Guard OEM key digest is SHA-384:

  BP.KEY = SHA384(LE(modulus) || LE(exponent))

The key manifest generated by coreboot's CBnT integration, however, hard
codes the SHA-256 public-key-hash algorithm for the KM regardless of the
platform.  For a Meteor Lake board whose vendor-provided KM correctly
declares SHA-384, the SHA-256 KM is the documented-wrong choice and does
not match the platform's expected OEM key digest.

The tree already defines the algorithm constants:

  PK_HASH_ALG_SHA1   := 4
  PK_HASH_ALG_SHA256 := 11
  PK_HASH_ALG_SHA384 := 12

Change the KM generation invocation from PK_HASH_ALG_SHA256 to
PK_HASH_ALG_SHA384 so the KM's KmPubKeyHashAlg field declares SHA-384.

Note: cbnt-prov's `km-show` will refuse the resulting manifest with
"KM public key hash algorithm must be SHA256".  That is a stale
pre-11th-generation rule hardcoded in the tool
(3rdparty/intel-sec-tools/pkg/intel/metadata/manifest/key.go), not a
platform requirement, and is intentionally not worked around here.

This affects all trees built from this Dasharo v5x0 fork; the preferred
long-term home is the Dasharo fork itself, or upstream coreboot.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
---
 src/security/intel/cbnt/Makefile.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/security/intel/cbnt/Makefile.mk b/src/security/intel/cbnt/Makefile.mk
index 19f75fdeaf..734207eb76 100644
--- a/src/security/intel/cbnt/Makefile.mk
+++ b/src/security/intel/cbnt/Makefile.mk
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@ $(obj)/km_unsigned.bin: $(obj)/km_pub.pem $(obj)/bpm_pub.pem $(CBNT_PROV)
 	$(CBNT_PROV) km-gen $@ $< --revision=$(CONFIG_INTEL_CBNT_KM_REVISION) \
 				--svn=$(CONFIG_INTEL_CBNT_KM_SVN) \
 				--id=$(CONFIG_INTEL_CBNT_KM_ID) \
-				--pkhashalg=$(PK_HASH_ALG_SHA256) \
+				--pkhashalg=$(PK_HASH_ALG_SHA384) \
 				--bpmpubkey=$(obj)/bpm_pub.pem \
 				--bpmhashalgo=$(PK_HASH_ALG_SHA256) \
 				--out=$(obj)/km_cfg.json
-- 
